1 NAME José Zeferino /Sáenz Hinojosa/
2 GIVN José Zeferino
2 SURN Sáenz Hinojosa
2 _MARNM Sáenz Hinojosa
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1760 AND 1778
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Con Un Pie En Cada Lado: Ethnicities and the Archaeology of Spanish Colonial Ranching Communities Along the Lower Río Grande Valley by Mary Jo Galindo:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://repositories.lib.utexas.edu/bitstream/handle/2152/589/galindomj039.pdf?se.
2 CONT
2 CONT Zeferino was a son of Miguel Saenz and Gertrudis Hinojosa, who apparently lived on the family ranch after his father received the family's land grant during the Visitation of 1767. Page 101 shows a partial rendition of the Saenz t
2 CONC ree in the generations following Miguel, identifying those families that resided at El Rancho San Pedro de Las Flores, a site located near or within present Roma, Texas. (Porcion 72 was awarded to Juan Angel Saenz, Miguel Saenz's 
2 CONC cousin and son of Miguel's Uncle Jose and first wife Teresa, and covers the western half of Roma, divided at the cemetery, stretching about 11 to 14 miles northward, apparently along Loma Blanca Road in rural Starr County. Porcion
2 CONC  73 was awarded to Miguel and his family. This grant takes up the eastern half of Roma, also stretching about 11 to 14 miles inland, parallel to Porcion 72, roughly along N. Ebony Avenue.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of marriage is listed according to citation given, but not birth or death of either Zeferino or spouse Rita, the latter of whom apparently comes from another branch of the Saenz family:
2 CONT *Spanish American Genealogical Association (SAGA) publications, 1989 Mier church marriage records, 1767-1925. Vols. 1 and 2. Spanish American Genealogical Society, Corpus Christi, Texas.
