2 CONT 24. JOSE-MATIAS5 LONGORIA-CHAPA (CLARA-MARIA4 CHAPA-BENAVIDES, JOSE-NICOLAS3 CHAPA-TREVINO, JUAN BAUTISTA2 CHAPA, BARTOLOME1 SCHIAPAPRIA) was born 1720 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, Mexico, and died Aft. 1798 in Camargo, Tamaulipas, Me
2 CONC xico. He married MARIA-MARGARITA HINOJOSA-DE-LA-GARZA Abt. 1745 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, Mexico, daughter of FRANCISCO HINOJOSA-DE-LA-GARZA and ANA LOPEZ-DE-JAEN. She wasborn 1720 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, Mexico, and died July 30,
2 CONC  1820 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JOSE-MATIAS LONGORIA-CHAPA:
2 CONT
2 CONT Founder of Camargo, Tamaulipas, Mexico
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his family are listed on the July 12th, 1757 census, Camargo, Tamaulipas, Mexico
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1798 he signed his last will and testament. This will can be found in the Seabury Papers collection which is housed at the University of Texas in Austin, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1767, he received from the King of Spain, the land grant known as Porcion 93 (7,971 acres). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the book, Mil Familias III, by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza, he is listed as a descendent of Don Alonso, de Estrada, the Duke of Aragon. Page 20.
2 CONT
2 CONT
