1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maria Nicolasa FLORES1704,1705 was born on 5 November 1778 in Camargo, Tamaulipas, New Spain.1706,1707 In the 1860 Census, there is a Nicolasa Longoria, 90 years old, at the home of Juan Longoria and his family. It
2 CONC  seems without doubt that this would be Juan's mother. However, if her age was 90 then, she would have been about 115 years old when she died about 1885. Moreover, she would have been about 30 years old when she had her first chil
2 CONC d, and around 50 years old when she had her last. My guess is that her age in the 1860 Census is in error; it seems more likely that she was around 80 years old then. However, Alma Rosa Guzman Cruz says that Nicolasa was just visi
2 CONC ting at Juan's home when the Census was taken, and that she did indeed live to be 115 years old. As further evidence of her longevity, Alma also claims that Adela Solis is currently 119 years old (as of August 2000) and still livi
2 CONC ng in a nursing home. In his last testament, Jose Antonio Flores named his children in the order I have listed here, omitting Manuel who died in 1785. Jose Antonio probably named his children from eldest to youngest; if this suppo
2 CONC sition is correct, then Maria Nicolasa was probably born around 1780 based on the fact that Maria Marcelina was baptized on May 4, 1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT UPDATE: A copy of her baptismal record (found by Irma Longoria Cavazos) indicates that Maria Nicolasa was baptized on November 25, 1778 and that she was 20 days old at the time. The discovery of her baptismal record fixes her birt
2 CONC hdate as November 5, 1778. Thus, she was about 106 years old when she died. She was baptized on 25 November 1778 in Camargo, Tamaulipas, New Spain.1707 Her godparents were Bartolo Flores and Maria Rita Vela. She died in 1885 at th
2 CONC e age of 107 in La Grulla, Starr County, TX, USA. From marker on grave. Maria was buried in La Grulla, Starr County, TX, USA.294 She is buried in the same vault as her grandson Eugenio Longoria, her son Juan Longoria, her daughter
2 CONC -in-law Yrinea Villarreal Longoria and her granddaughter Yrinea Longoria Garcia. She was from Las Cuevitas. Parents: Jose Antonio FLORES and Isabel SALINAS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Pedro Jose LONGORIA Villarreal. Maria Nicolasa FLORES and Pedro Jose LONGORIA Villarreal were married on 6 July 1798 in Reynosa, Tamaulipas, New Spain.1708 They settled in the El Tepeguaje and La Laja ranches in Mexico. Af
2 CONC ter Pedro died, Maria Nicolasa went to live with her son Juan. Children were: Zenobio LONGORIA Flores, Eugenio LONGORIA Flores, Nepomuceno LONGORIA Flores, Juan Jose LONGORIA Flores, Juan Santiago LONGORIA Flores, Jose Tomas LONGO
2 CONC RIA Flores, Pedro Jose LONGORIA Flores, Martin LONGORIA Flores, Barbara LONGORIA Flores, Catarina LONGORIA Flores.
2 CONT
