1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Raul N. Longoria's Genealogy Database:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b88.html#P1423
2 CONT
2 CONT Jose Maria GARCIA SALINAS [1897] was born (date unknown). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jose Maria Garcia Salinas was the Original Grantee of the Laureles, a 4 league tract in what is now Nueces County. He was the brother of Rafael Garcia Salinas, Original Grantee of the La Mestena y Gonzalena 5-league tract in Brook
2 CONC s County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Leocadia SAENZ. Leocadia SAENZ and Jose Maria GARCIA SALINAS were married. Children were: 
2 CONT *1. Santos GARCIA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnote:
2 CONT *1897. Family Tree Book (The F. W. Seabury Papers), a transcription of the original papers in The Center for American History at The University of Texas at Austin, transcribed and edited by Joel Rene Escobar, New Santander Press, 
2 CONC Edinburg, TX, 1995, Page 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Texas State Historical Association:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/online/articles/apl04
2 CONT
2 CONT The Laureles Ranch, on an old Spanish grant twenty-two miles south of Corpus Christi, was acquired from the heirs of the original grantee by Mifflin Kenedy, partner in the King Ranch from 1860 to 1868 with Richard King. José Pérez
2 CONC  Rey and María José Pérez Rey named the grant Rincón de los Laureles, "Corner of the Laurels," probably from groves of laurels that were growing there.
