1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 FEB 1801
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cerralvo
3 STAE Nuevo Reino de León
3 CTRY Virreinato de Nueva España
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Jose Antonio Chapa (0503) is the legitimate son of Joseph Xavier Chapa (0400) and Maria Josefa Saucedo. Jose Antonio Chapa married Maria del Refugio Salinas in the parish church at Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, on January
2 CONC  27, 1783. Maria del Refugio Salinas is the legitimate daughter of Teodor Salinas and Josefa Sosa. Jose Antonio died February 11, 1798 at Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of Jose Antonio Chapa (0503) and Maria del Refugio Salinas, extracted from the Cerralvo Birth Records, follow.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1784/02/23 Ma. Felipa de Jesus (0610) Jose Antonio Chapa
2 CONT  Chapa Ma. del Refugio Salinas
2 CONT
2 CONT 1786/04/20 Jose Simon Chapa (0611) Jose Antonio Chapa
2 CONT  Ma. del Refugio Salinas
2 CONT
2 CONT 1790/12/19 Josefa Francisca Chapa (0612) Jose Antonio Chapa
2 CONT  Ma. del Refugio Salinas
2 CONT
2 CONT 1793/03/09 Ma. Gertrudis Chapa (0613) Jose Antonio Chapa
2 CONT  1794/07/03 Died Ma. del Refugio Salinas
2 CONT
2 CONT 1795/05/31 Ma. Gertrudis Chapa (0614) Jose Antonio Chapa
2 CONT  Ma. del Refugio Salinas
2 CONT
2 CONT 1797/07/29 Jose Maria Chapa (0615) Jose Antonio Chapa
2 CONT  Ma. del Refugio Salinas
2 CONT
2 CONT 1799/10/23 Jose Dionicio Chapa (5525) Jose Antonio Chapa
2 CONT  Ma. del Refugio Salinas
2 CONT
2 CONT  ANALYSIS OF JOSE ANTONIO CHAPA
2 CONT
2 CONT Jose Antonio Chapa (5420) and Maria Encarnacion Barrera were married January 7, 1784, according to an LDS microfilm index of the CHAPA baptisms and marriages in Nuevo Leon. The same index lists them as the parents of nine children
2 CONC . Assuming that a man normally marries around twenty, Jose Antonio Chapa (5420) would have been born circa 1764.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reviewing my CHAPA databank for a Jose Antonio Chapa born around 1764, I found only one other that could possibly be same man. Jose Antonio Chapa (0503) the son of Jose Xavier Chapa and Maria Josefa Saucedo, married Maria del Refu
2 CONC gio Salinas on January 27, 1783, at Cerralvo. This marriage produced at least seven children so he could not possibly marry Maria Encarnacion in 1784.
2 CONT
2 CONT LDS film # 1162851 is a secondary document. After the turn of the twentieth century, Mexico had a project to copy their old baptism, marriage, and death records. Men were hired to catalogue and abstract those old records. There ar
2 CONC e many mistakes in the transcriptions and when question arise one should consult the primary document if at all possible. Note that the secondary record indicates that the parents of Jose Antonio Chapa (5420) are Javier Chapa and 
2 CONC Josefa de la Garza. Javier and Xavier is a spelling variation. Marie Josefa Saucedo and Josefa de la Garza could be an error in the surnames. The match of the mother's given name, the same father, and a close agreement on birthday
2 CONC s leads me to conclude that Jose Antonio Chapa (5420) and (0503) are one and the same, however, the marriage data above prevents that conclusion.
2 CONT
2 CONT Further, Jose Xavier Chapa (0400) the son of Agustin Xavier Chapa (0300) and Antonia Margarita Guajardo could not have been married to a Josefa de la Garza since his children with Maria Josefa Saucedo were born between 1760 and 17
2 CONC 80. Josefa de la Garza's son, Jose Antonio Chapa, was born circa 1764.
2 CONT
2 CONT If I now assume that the mother's name, Maria Josefa de la Garza, is correct I can find only one marriage to a Jose Gregorio Chapa (2510). They did have a son Jose Antonio Chapa (2661) who was born in August 23, 1761 and could pos
2 CONC sibly marry Maria Encarnacion Barrera 23 years later. This assumption requires that an error in the father's given name was recorded. I am not ready to make this leap yet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Norman P. Brown
2 CONT  October 1, 1990
2 CONT
